<Base title="Privacy Notice | Kubernautic" description="How personal data may be processed when visiting the Kubernautic website.">
<section class="shell page-hero legal-hero"><span class="eyebrow">PRIVACY</span><h1>Privacy notice<span class="gradient-text">.</span></h1><p>Information about personal data processing on kubernautic.com.</p></section>
<section class="shell section legal-section"><article class="contact-card legal-copy">
<p class="legal-date">Last updated: 16 November 2026</p>
<h2>1. Controller</h2>
<p>Kubernauts GmbH<br />Im Mediapark 4C, 50670 Cologne, Germany<br />Email: <a href="mailto:contact@kubernauts.de">contact@kubernauts.de</a><br />Telephone: +49 221 379 90 680</p>
<h2>2. Website access and hosting</h2>
<p>The public kubernautic.com website is delivered through GitHub Pages. Cloudflare is used for domain services and potentially network services. When you access the website, technical information may be processed, such as IP address, access time, requested URL, browser and device details, and HTTP response status. These data may be necessary to deliver and protect the website, diagnose faults, and prevent abuse.</p>
<p>Where applicable, the legal basis is Article 6(1)(f) GDPR (legitimate interests in reliable and secure website operation). Providers may process data outside the European Economic Area, subject to applicable international-transfer safeguards. Actual technical-log retention depends on the service providers and configured settings.</p>
<h2>3. Externally loaded fonts</h2>
<p>The website currently loads Google Fonts CSS and font files. Your browser may establish a direct connection to Google servers to retrieve these resources, which may transmit your IP address and technical request information. We are reviewing local font hosting to avoid these external requests.</p>
<h2>4. Cookies, analytics and advertising</h2>
<p>The current static product website is not designed to collect registrations, process payments, or operate its own analytics or advertising trackers. External services may process technically necessary data. Whether cookies or comparable storage technologies are used depends on the actual deployed implementation and services. If non-essential tracking technologies are introduced, any required consent mechanism will be implemented before activation.</p>
<h2>5. Console preview, demo and external services</h2>
<p>This notice covers the public product website. Separately operated Console, demo, registration, or future trial services may involve different data flows and require additional privacy information. When you deliberately follow links to third-party websites such as OpenKubes or GitHub, their privacy notices also apply.</p>
<h2>6. Email inquiries</h2>
<p>When you contact us by email, we process the information you provide to respond to your inquiry. Depending on the request, the legal basis is Article 6(1)(b) or (f) GDPR. Information is retained only as long as required for the inquiry or applicable legal obligations.</p>
<h2>7. Your rights</h2>
<p>Subject to applicable legal requirements, you may request access, correction, erasure, restriction, portability, and object to processing. Consent, where given, can be withdrawn for the future. You may also complain to a competent data protection authority. Please direct privacy questions to <a href="mailto:contact@kubernauts.de">contact@kubernauts.de</a>.</p>
<h2>8. Updates</h2>
<p>We update this notice if our services, data processing, or legal requirements change.</p>
<p class="legal-related"><a href="/imprint/">View imprint →</a></p>
</article></section>
